{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01703",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.07,
      "end_seconds": 4.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Hi, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.63,
      "end_seconds": 9.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.72,
      "end_seconds": 16.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got swollen glands in my neck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.87,
      "end_seconds": 22.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.57,
      "end_seconds": 27.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "It's been two days, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.73,
      "end_seconds": 31.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.33,
      "end_seconds": 46.08,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "Okay, so I'd call it moderate. And there's a fever as well, two weeks now. About fever, it feels moderate to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.37,
      "end_seconds": 53.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.75,
      "end_seconds": 68.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.34,
      "end_seconds": 98.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.36,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 117 over 80, temp 38.1 degrees, SpO2 95 percent on room air, respiratory rate 20, pulse is 101 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.01,
      "end_seconds": 103.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.9,
      "end_seconds": 121.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.12,
      "end_seconds": 124.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.47,
      "end_seconds": 148.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Your tonsils are large with white coating and the glands in the neck are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.08,
      "end_seconds": 162.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.09,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Have you had any difficulty breathing, rash or tummy pain on the left?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.26,
      "end_seconds": 171.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Erm, um, I haven't had difficulty breathing, rash or tummy pain on the left, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.15,
      "end_seconds": 176.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.98,
      "end_seconds": 181.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.98,
      "end_seconds": 184.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.62,
      "end_seconds": 189.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.41,
      "end_seconds": 193.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.35,
      "end_seconds": 198.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.2,
      "end_seconds": 209.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.93,
      "end_seconds": 214.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "I take throat lozenges, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.27,
      "end_seconds": 219.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Understood. Alright, have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.07,
      "end_seconds": 224.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Not currently, but as a youngster amoxicillin gave me hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.65,
      "end_seconds": 247.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "So, any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.22,
      "end_seconds": 249.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Not really, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.84,
      "end_seconds": 278.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.89,
      "text": "Putting it all together, I'd lean towards glandular fever. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.92,
      "end_seconds": 283.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.36,
      "end_seconds": 313.93,
      "duration_seconds": 29.57,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now glandular fever is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let's book a blood count to look into glandular fever. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Rest, plenty of fluids, and no contact sport for a month because of the spleen. Let's plan a check in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.74,
      "end_seconds": 318.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.29,
      "end_seconds": 323.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.74,
      "end_seconds": 329.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}